Falsifies `capability_table::the_peak_never_falls_and_a_floor_insert_stays_above_its_floor`.

The defect: `first_free_from` shifts its mask the wrong way, so the lowest free slot "at or above
the floor" is the lowest free slot below the end of the floor's complement, and a floor insert can
land under its floor.

Expected to fail: `assert!(slot >= floor, "a floor insert landed below its floor")`, on any table
with a free slot below a nonzero floor.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -364,7 +364,7 @@
             (first..Self::WORDS).find_map(|word| {
                 // The first word drops the slots below the floor; the words after it count whole.
                 let bits = if word == first {
-                    self.free[word] & (u64::MAX << (floor % WORD_BITS))
+                    self.free[word] & (u64::MAX >> (floor % WORD_BITS))
                 } else {
                     self.free[word]
                 };
